{"authored" [{"question" "e-21585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/d8be54eddd0358742170a03b3c55e0cb94eaf2a7d59f12e1c4361a6197d29847.png)\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\ln 2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/example-21585.json" "file_sha256" "cd58e5d025795c8c1399930d5af84e67bb9a47fdeab3787f0cfd0ffd24d77804" "basis" 2279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\ln 2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot 2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2(12)+1(4) \\\\ 1(12)+2(4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24+4 \\\\ 12+8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/example-21585.json" "file_sha256" "cd58e5d025795c8c1399930d5af84e67bb9a47fdeab3787f0cfd0ffd24d77804" "basis" 2279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/example-21586.json" "file_sha256" "8c38af3435ad03e4ba02af70e0318f88c80bd2870bf5246326490440231050f5" "basis" 2279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which $x' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n3x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = 3x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which $y' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-2x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = -2x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/66cdd05ac68d762c5b78df40b22f9e0cd660099c13e48e9eb71c81c73a044280.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/example-21586.json" "file_sha256" "8c38af3435ad03e4ba02af70e0318f88c80bd2870bf5246326490440231050f5" "basis" 2279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown below (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Sketch the trajectory of the solution starting at the marked point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/0cf7942e618f0465ead5b98c6404a3747e505db75517725971c833c97121ab64.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/example-21588.json" "file_sha256" "c3871ee034843d3fbf1a4042057abf22b9dc8ffd2b2df7009d895a6099724f99" "basis" 2279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, moving along with the flow (downward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/105bdbdcac5f0ff20f71a0131bf5bb3cbafe0e93ce8bc733a51c2dcb3fb8364f.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues downward, but the trajectory starts to turn slightly to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/96757a3aee3b161b2ba9887cd85f977f063807779604647dd791cf265790cabc.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues to go downwards and slightly to the left to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/658c15d2291368d0e6836ba19b90157d49dee4a510d58cddf7f85ddc9ff72a8d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/example-21588.json" "file_sha256" "c3871ee034843d3fbf1a4042057abf22b9dc8ffd2b2df7009d895a6099724f99" "basis" 2279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-331275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(1,-2)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-331275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(1,-2)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =2x-2y \\\\  & =2(1)-2(-2) \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =2x-3y \\\\  & =2(1)-3(-2) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-331275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-331275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-331275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-331275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+9[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)(\\frac{2}{3})+0(-36) \\\\ 0\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3})+2(-36)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-72 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(3,-1)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(3,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =-x+4y \\\\  & =-3+4(-1) \\\\  & =-3-4 \\\\  & =-7 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =2x+2y \\\\  & =2(3)+2(-1) \\\\  & =6-2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(1,-1)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(1,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =5x-y \\\\  & =5(1)-(-1) \\\\  & =5+1 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =-x-2y \\\\  & =-1-2(-1) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2(12)+1(8) \\\\ 0(12)+3(8)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24+8 \\\\ 0+24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}32 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}32 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}32 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n2x+4y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/59a731b27e2333fef2bfa48e9e61a7075548ddd74782c1fadf1dd98f68ef2a7e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "2x"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4x"] ["math" "-x"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}x"] ["math" "x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332647" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-3x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=3x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/b6eb04363e97559b51ae43439d965eb19fd7f6acca57916f3159317ceba033ba.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "2x"] ["math" "x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3x"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}x"] ["math" "3x"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332639" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-x-y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n3x-2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/3b064f5f1b2e1a2c8bc3146b4b44a8d2e7b0ab7a83856488bde00ac6ab875efe.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x"] ["math" "-x"] ["math" "2x"] ["math" "x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3x"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}x"] ["math" "3x"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332658" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-5x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-5x+2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{5}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/077f785b498c69dfe131ca766df7bad71600e4c7ac28c5a8013603bc56e3be10.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "2x"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5x"] ["math" "-x"] ["math" "5x"] ["math" "x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332661" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-2x+4y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx-y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/19c33a634af36765142e2f4b85df1b9209d3f1abf105a131b629b3249bd91c2c.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332634" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3952ac3e72d16baf204352e641b94778a63aa5cf917e6243634d622c4b644385"} {"question" "q-332634" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332634" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2x"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "2x"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/state.json" "file_sha256" "70d8e6e9a8536ec73d6f1f7a902f0885c5e0495e1d412bdbe360fe1fcc84a4e4"} {"question" "q-332634" "field" "field-1" "attribu