21585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/d8be54eddd0358742170a03b3c55e0cb94eaf2a7d59f12e1c4361a6197d29847.png)\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\ln 2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/example-21585.json" "file_sha256" "970afd23935a995d90302472e1b45af493ec754bd480c9efd7a8d93d95f8d7ff"} {"question" "e-21585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\ln 2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot 2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2(12)+1(4) \\\\ 1(12)+2(4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24+4 \\\\ 12+8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/example-21585.json" "file_sha256" "970afd23935a995d90302472e1b45af493ec754bd480c9efd7a8d93d95f8d7ff"} {"question" "e-21586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/example-21586.json" "file_sha256" "c738600b6598f59a9400b10d1ceb5a8c30a31f2d838b57dee0380d3e44915506"} {"question" "e-21586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which $x' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n3x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = 3x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which $y' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-2x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = -2x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/66cdd05ac68d762c5b78df40b22f9e0cd660099c13e48e9eb71c81c73a044280.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/example-21586.json" "file_sha256" "c738600b6598f59a9400b10d1ceb5a8c30a31f2d838b57dee0380d3e44915506"} {"question" "e-21588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown below (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Sketch the trajectory of the solution starting at the marked point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/0cf7942e618f0465ead5b98c6404a3747e505db75517725971c833c97121ab64.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/example-21588.json" "file_sha256" "a6657de172ccf1a2b783a9c53eaea66586801cdc7e79316644f48ae7d277c4c0"} {"question" "e-21588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, moving along with the flow (downward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/105bdbdcac5f0ff20f71a0131bf5bb3cbafe0e93ce8bc733a51c2dcb3fb8364f.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues downward, but the trajectory starts to turn slightly to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/96757a3aee3b161b2ba9887cd85f977f063807779604647dd791cf265790cabc.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues to go downwards and slightly to the left to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/658c15d2291368d0e6836ba19b90157d49dee4a510d58cddf7f85ddc9ff72a8d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/example-21588.json" "file_sha256" "a6657de172ccf1a2b783a9c53eaea66586801cdc7e79316644f48ae7d277c4c0"}] "usage" {"q-331275" [] "e-21588" [] "e-21586" [] "e-21585" []} "basis" 2310 "retractions" [[17592186167131 :question/problem "${x^{′}(t) = 2x(t) - 2y(t); y^{′}(t) = 2x(t) - 3y(t)$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(1,-2)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?"] [17592186166465 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/d8be54eddd0358742170a03b3c55e0cb94eaf2a7d59f12e1c4361a6197d29847.png)\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\ln 2?$"] [17592186166466 :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which $x' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n3x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = 3x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which $y' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-2x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = -2x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/66cdd05ac68d762c5b78df40b22f9e0cd660099c13e48e9eb71c81c73a044280.png)"] [17592186166467 :question/problem "A sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown below (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Sketch the trajectory of the solution starting at the marked point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/0cf7942e618f0465ead5b98c6404a3747e505db75517725971c833c97121ab64.png)"] [17592186166467 :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, moving along with the flow (downward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/105bdbdcac5f0ff20f71a0131bf5bb3cbafe0e93ce8bc733a51c2dcb3fb8364f.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues downward, but the trajectory starts to turn slightly to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/96757a3aee3b161b2ba9887cd85f977f063807779604647dd791cf265790cabc.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues to go downwards and slightly to the left to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068149/assets/658c15d2291368d0e6836ba19b90157d49dee4a510d58cddf7f85ddc9ff72a8d.png)"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186164144 17592186164145 17592186164146 17592186164147 17592186164148] "immutable_fields" [[17592186164143 :answer-field/correct] [17592186164143 :answer-field/id] [17592186164143 :answer-field/key] [17592186164143 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
